<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="4bd370af">&lt;p&gt;
    A variance between the expected benefits of a program or project versus the actual realized benefits may be due to:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Some intended benefits are not being realized at all.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Some intended benefits are being realized but not as per the expectations of the stakeholders and as documented in
        the Business Case.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Benefits&amp;nbsp;Realization team&amp;nbsp;ensures timely reporting, tracking and validation of benefits with benefits owners
    for allocated benefits. Driver based analytics should be carried out to determine the root cause of issues and
    challenges in realizing the benefits. Discuss benefits register with benefits owners to determine the frequency and
    dates for measurement while aggregating and validating the benefits. Gathers data across the program and leverage
    predictive analytics and statistical analysis to determine challenges realizing benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    If cost, benefits and risks&amp;nbsp;change over time,&amp;nbsp;it requires a continuously updated business case.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="d4e1e36d"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="f5f0df13"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="451483bc"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="5861ca53">To highlight the differences (if any) between the&amp;nbsp;expected benefits of a program or project&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;ones
that&amp;nbsp;are being&amp;nbsp;realized. The findings of this task allow the program or project team to keep the leadership
informed and craft out specific corrective action plans.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="9fa011c6"></attribute>
